{
  "comment": "wb-byfw cut #4 (the R-B394 fail-closed core over cut #3's roster: refusal #2 U3, the R-B362 enumerate-the-resolvable form; the R660 / wb-5jha roster shape): the out-of-file anchor for the judged rows' ids, readings and case texts of test/workbench-hyperunix-document-witness-census.test.ts - every W3 TWIN_CONTROLS row with its readBy, path, calls and the sha256 of its probe's and its present's initializer text as the census spells it, every W4 site with its form's twin, every W7 PROXY_FORMS row with its throwBy, readBy, path and the same two digests, every W8 READER_PAGES page with its lead count, its forms and the sha256 of its page text, every W9 CASE_PAGES page with its row and shared counts and the sha256 of its source, and the shared declarations the W3 and W7 rows' probes and presents name with the sha256 of each statement's text, in census order, as read at the cut. The census's ROSTER case requires its in-file tables and caseReading's reading of its own source to equal these lists exactly, both ways and in order, and its RECORDS case expects a case under the id of every row, site and page listed here; the digests are of text, so a case run on a row changed at run time, or handed an it.each table argument other than its table's rows, is NOT CLAIMED (the census header's SCOPE and NOT CLAIMED; wb-gnj9 carries the W3 and W7 route).",
